(FLW-42: the exit code is 0 to 255; a code computed outside that range
 when the program runs exits with 255 (LANGUAGE.md:2423-2426). `code`
 holds two numbers over the program, so the compiler cannot prove its
 value and the check happens at run time. The code may be a variable.
 A code the compiler CAN prove is refused instead: `Exit 300.` and
 `quit -1.` each fail to compile with "cannot exit with code 300" (or -1)
 and the note "an exit code is between 0 and 255" (hand-run 2026-10-13).
 Up to vox 0.4.15 the code was taken modulo 256 and this probe was
 `Exit 300.`, exiting 44. Re-recorded 2026-10-13 on vox main a0a2ecc.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox FLW-42.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   before
   exit 255
)
a number called code is 7.
Set code to code add 293.
print "before".
